  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 113 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nMinimally impactful weather is expected through next weekend. Mostly \ncloudy skies will remain across the region tonight as breezy \nnortheast wind stream over the relativity warm waters of Lakes \nMichigan and Superior, however, with increasing dry air moving in at \nmid-levels don't expect any lake effect rain. A short-wave, \ncurrently over Wyoming, will track east across the mid-Mississippi \nand Ohio valleys Monday and Tuesday shutting warm and moist air well \nsouth of the region and allowing a Hudson Bay high to continue \nfeeding seasonally cool, dry, and stable air into the region. With \nthat clear skies over night Monday and Tuesday nights may lead to \nareas of frost across parts of north-central WI. Temperatures will \nbegin to trend warmer later into the week with highs return to above \nnormal by next weekend. Next chance for widespread rain doesn't look \nto arrive until early next week.",
